{#- Caddy reverse proxy with the caddy-dns/porkbun plugin, one container
   (formulas/podman). The stock image has no DNS plugins, so the image is
   built on the minion itself (files/Containerfile, xcaddy) and tagged
   localhost/<built_image>:<tag>-porkbun<porkbun_version> — no registry, so
   no chicken-and-egg with a registry behind this very Caddy. Built only when
   that tag is missing; bumping either version rebuilds and restarts.
   image/tag: the upstream base (Renovate bumps it via the map.jinja regex);
   the builder stage uses <tag>-builder. porkbun_version: Go module version
   (Renovate, go datasource).

   uid/gid: the container runs as this system account (Podman User=, mapped
   1:1), so data_dir (certificates, ACME account) stays owned by it. The
   matching formulas/users account entry (pillar) must use the same numbers.
   Listens on 8443/8080 inside (non-root, no CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE),
   published on https_port/http_port; :80 only redirects to https. Caddy's
   own redirect would carry the inner port, so it's off and an explicit
   http:// site redirects instead.

   domain: the wildcard zone (*.<domain>, one certificate via DNS-01).
   routes: [{name, upstream, auth}] -> https://<name>.<domain> proxied to
   upstream; anything else under the wildcard gets a 404.
   forward_auth: upstream of an auth server (Authentik's embedded outpost,
   http://authentik-server:9000). Empty = off; when set, routes with
   auth: forward go through it first.
   acme_email: optional ACME account contact.
   resolvers: DNS servers Caddy asks to see its TXT record propagate (the
   challenge check), public ones so the LAN resolver's cache doesn't matter.
   metrics_port: Prometheus /metrics, plain HTTP, published on the host.

   porkbun_api_key / porkbun_secret_api_key: required, pillar fills them  secret-scan: allow (doc text)
   from OpenBao (porkbun/api); config.sls fails without them.

   network: the Podman network Caddy shares with the apps it fronts on the
   same host (Authentik, step 6).
   podman: spec overrides for the container (keys: formulas/podman README). #}
{%- set public_resolvers = ['1.1.1.1', '9.9.9.9'] %}{#- secret-scan: allow (public DNS resolvers) #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'image': 'docker.io/library/caddy',
    'tag': '2.11.9',
    'porkbun_version': 'v0.3.1',
    'built_image': 'localhost/caddy-porkbun',
    'container_name': 'caddy',
    'network': 'edge',
    'uid': 978,
    'gid': 978,
    'base_dir': '/opt/caddy',
    'build_dir': '/opt/caddy/build',
    'config_dir': '/opt/caddy/config',
    'data_dir': '/opt/caddy/data',
    'state_dir': '/opt/caddy/state',
    'https_port': 443,
    'http_port': 80,
    'metrics_port': 9180,
    'domain': '',
    'routes': [],
    'forward_auth': '',
    'acme_email': '',
    'resolvers': public_resolvers,
    'porkbun_api_key': '',
    'porkbun_secret_api_key': '',
    'podman': {},
} %}
{%- set caddy = salt['pillar.get']('caddy:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
{%- do caddy.update({'ref_tag': caddy.tag ~ '-porkbun' ~ caddy.porkbun_version | replace('v', '', 1)}) %}
